// Curated example builds for the "Build guides" page.
//
// Every build here is machine-verified against the real availability logic
// (gearAvailability.js/isGearItemAvailable) under its own regions + relics, so
// an implementer can render these directly and trust that:
//   - the three blessings are one per tier and `godTier` is what
//     resolveGodTier() actually returns for them
//   - `regions` is exactly 3 optional picks (Misthalin/Karamja/Havenhythe are
//     always free and are NOT listed)
//   - `relics` is at most 1 tier-1 relic plus at most 2 unknown-tier relics
//   - every item name in `loadouts` exists in gear.js AND is available under
//     that build's regions+relics
//   - no loadout pairs a two-handed weapon with an off-hand
//
// The loadouts were generated by an ordered per-slot preference list rather
// than chosen by eye, then validated - see `opus combat notes/08-build-corrections.md`
// for the rules encoded, and 09-generated-loadouts.json for the raw output.
//
// RULES BAKED IN (all from user review + `07-gear-research.md`):
//   - Late-game armour must be AUGMENTABLE. Primal, base Teralith/Tempest/
//     Primeval and Starbloom are not, so they are mid-late only; Achto
//     Teralith/Tempest, Cryptbloom, Vestments of Havoc, Torva and Elite
//     Tectonic/Dracolich are.
//   - Cape is always Igneous: the style-specific Kal-Ket/Xil/Mej/Mor (t85)
//     mid-late, the combined Kal-Zuk (t95, +37.1 to all four styles) late.
//     Never a max cape - it is only +30 and Igneous is free from Misthalin.
//   - Pocket is a crit item (Erethdor's grimoire +12%, Chaotic grimoire +7%)
//     or a god Scripture. NEVER the Underworld Grimoire, which is a skilling
//     item with no combat effect at all.
//   - Ammo is always equipped. `min(t_weapon, t_ammo)` caps ability damage, so
//     an empty ammo slot is a silent DPS loss.
//   - No Masterwork or Trimmed Masterwork anywhere - far too slow to make.
//   - Exactly 3 regions, never Fremennik.
//   - Tirannwn means killing Solak, so it never appears on a difficulty-1 build.
//
// `armourTotal` is precomputed with utils/gearStats.js's STYLE-AWARE
// getArmourRating plus getSkillArmour(99) = 1212.24, ceiled - i.e. exactly the
// Total Armour the gear planner would show.
//
// `armourTotalOverloaded` is the same sum at 99 + 17 Defence, because an
// OVERLOAD GIVES +17 DEFENCE and armour from the Defence skill is
// D^3/1250 + 4D + 40. That is 1212.24 -> 1752.72, so simply being overloaded is
// worth about +540 armour before any gear. It matters enormously here because
// four blessings scale off total armour, and you are overloaded for essentially
// all PvM - so the overloaded figure is the honest one for DPS purposes:
//   Teragard's Aegis (x3)  +405 ability damage
//   Striking Light (250%)  +1,351 per Light of Saradomin
//   Steadfast Will Bash    +2,162
//   Barkscales (10%)       +54 flat damage reduction
//
// `armourTotalElder` is the same sum at 99 + 25 Defence, because an ELDER
// OVERLOAD gives +25 rather than +17 - and it boosts your main combat stat by
// the same amount, which feeds the 2.5*f(level) term of the ability damage
// formula as well. Elder overloads are Meilyr potions, reachable from
// TIRANNWN (Prifddinas) or the DIVINE DRUID relic, which unlocks every Meilyr
// recipe. Every build here has one route or the other, and The Ironclad and
// The Shieldbearer have both.
//
// BASIC ATTACKS ARE NOT EQUAL ACROSS STYLES (runescape.wiki/w/Basic_attacks):
//   melee  110-130% (avg 120%)  + generates a Bloodlust stack
//   magic   90-110% (avg 100%)
//   ranged  90-110% (avg 100%)  - but Dark bow / Gloomfire bow hit TWICE at
//                                 45-55% each, which matters for any per-hit
//                                 effect (Abyssal Cinders, Big Boned)
//   necro   90-110% (avg 100%)
// Melee is 20% ahead of every other style, so Striking Light's +40% to basic
// attacks is worth proportionally more on a melee bar than anywhere else.
//
// Versus no overload at all, an Elder overload is worth:
//   armour            1212.24 -> 2061.30  (+849)
//   Aegis x3 (75%)    +637 ability damage
//   main stat +25     +55 ability damage (2.5*f(99)=264 -> 2.5*f(124)=319)
//   COMBINED          +692 ability damage
//   Striking Light    +2,123 per Light of Saradomin
//   Steadfast Bash    +3,396
// That is comparable to a whole gear tier, from a potion - so it is surfaced on
// every loadout rather than left as an assumption.
//
// ARTEFACT-ONLY REGION GROUPS ARE NOT TREATED AS GATING. A few Arch relics
// (Death Ward, Hungry Like the Wolf, Inspire Awe) list a second region that is
// only needed to physically excavate that dig site's artefacts. Those materials
// can be obtained without ever visiting the region - via the Archaeology
// Research system, via Thieving, or from tetracompass digs - so they are
// verified with `ignoreArtefactRegions: true`, matching the Relics page's own
// "Artefacts are not region-locked" toggle. `ARTEFACT_BYPASS_NOTE` below is the
// user-facing explanation; surface it wherever an artefact-gated relic appears.

// Per-relic accent colours for the relic pills. Distinct from the red/green/
// blue blessing palette, which encodes something else on the same card.
