      "Play it exactly like Teragard's Bulwark - shield up, Preparation and Revenge held on cooldown, Bash woven in. The difference is what you stack: favour damage bonus over raw armour where the two conflict, because Abyssal Cinders pays 15% of ability damage on every single hit and your rotation produces a great many hits. Lead with multi-hit abilities and Rapid Fire.",
    tradeoffs: [
      'Forfeits Bow of the Last Guardian and its Perfect Equilibrium passive.',
      'Solak (for Erethdor\'s grimoire) and the Mazcab raid (for Achto Tempest) are both serious bosses - this build has the longest runway of the shield trio.',
      'Elite Dracolich\'s crit set effect is bow-only, so it is not an option alongside a crossbow.',
    ],
    keyNumbers: [
      { label: 'Total armour (late)', value: '3,605 - 4,454 elder overloaded' },
      { label: 'Elder overload worth', value: '+692 ability damage (both routes)' },
      { label: 'Abyssal Cinders per hit', value: '+594' },
      { label: "Erethdor's grimoire", value: '+12% crit chance' },
    ],
